The set of Mode 01 PIDs omatach ships is bounded by the Service 01 table in the
Wikipedia article "OBD-II PIDs" (https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OBD-II_PIDs),
licensed CC BY-SA 4.0. Only the PID numbers follow that article; the datapoint
names, units, ranges and decode equations in data/j1979_catalog.json are Grey
Horse Software's own work. See data/PROVENANCE.md.

data/dtcs.json contains diagnostic trouble code descriptions: generic codes as
defined by SAE J2012, and manufacturer-defined codes for Ford, FCA and GM.
Manufacturer names are used for identification only. All trademarks are the
property of their owners, and omatach is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or a
product of any vehicle manufacturer.

"OBDLink" is a trademark of OCTech / ScanTool.net. "Torque" refers to the Torque
Android app's equation dialect, which obd_equation_rs implements independently
for compatibility; Torque is a trademark of its owner. omatach is an independent
product and is not affiliated with either.
